  "about": "Facts code fills in, so the AI never has to guess them. aliases = ways people write the name (split the way the code splits words: 'iphone 5 s'); not_if = words that mean it is a different model; storage/colours/options = the only values that exist (special editions count as colours); colour_aliases = shorter ways people write a colour; colour_words = plain colours that are part of a special edition's design (the 30th Anniversary PS5 is grey); colour_rules = editions that only come one way; confirm_with = words one of which must also appear, because the plain name fits another model too (confirm_why says what to add); specs = facts that never change for the model; sources = where they were checked. Only the models AlertFlip (the owner's marketplace-alert app) covers are listed: any other model goes to 'needs you'. iPhones checked against Apple UK (support.apple.com/en-gb/108044, apple.com/uk/iphone/compare) on 28 Oct 2026; the rest against Samsung, PlayStation and Nintendo pages the same day.",
